        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Here is a little bit more to add:</P><P>Giant Faction<BR>Kromzek -most giants are of this faction includes guards<BR>Kromrif -vendors and quest givers<BR>King tormax -king tormax(go figure) and his guards.</P><P>Most people start off KOS to giants, Kromzek is easy to raise Kromrif far more difficult King tormax even more so.</P><P>Dragon<BR>Claws of Veeshan -most dragons including guards<BR>Yelinak - Merchants and quest givers</P><P>Dragon faction is difficult faction to raise (at least it is for a DE necro of Inny) as far as I know the merchant faction can only be raised thru quest?</P><P>Dwarf<BR>Coldain - My best guess that its pretty much all dwarfs are on this faction<BR>Dain frostreaver IV - ? leader of the codain? Im not sure how it ties into doing business with the Dwarfs???</P><P>Plus and minus.<BR>The Dwarfs and Dragons seem to be allied with each other so in general killing stuff to raise faction with one will most likely raise the faction of the other. Killing giants will most often raise faction of both.<BR>Dwarfs are very easy to get in good with dragons much less so. It seems to me that the dwarf quest and the Dragon quest yield about the same quality of equipment. <BR>I decided that I want to get in good with dragons and dwarfs and the following is my biggest reason why.<BR>WUOSHI!!!!!!! -Claws of Veeshan and Yelinak factions, lvl 64 dragon, huge Aggro radius equals instant death to anyone on his bad side.  He seems to be up about half the time in the Wakening lands where he hangs out at the Teleport spot. So if you have bad Dragon faction especially if your a wizzy or a druid then kiss the wakening spell good bye and dont even mem it. if you want to get to some of the best hunting areas of Velious just plan on a very long run from iceclad. </P><P>Giant <BR>Very complex faction system. Dont even think that when your on the good side of Kromzek that you can explore the city at leisure, you might still be kos to Kromrif, and once you do lots of faction work to get good with kromrif, you might be KOS to king tormax. However, I have been told that the quest given out by giants result for the most part in better items.</P><P>To help us plan for future raids please state the faction(s) you want to keep in good with.</P><P>For me I am going with the Dwarf/Dragon faction</P><P>Reix Tyrannus<BR>Necromancer 54th lvl</P><P>Edited by - reix on 10 Apr 2001  16:02:01<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
